# Canonical identity for people who appear under more than one email address.
#
# GitHub keys contributor attribution on the author email, so one person who has
# committed from two addresses is counted as two contributors. This file tells
# git - and GitHub - that those addresses are the same person.
#
# Format: <proper-name> <proper-email> <commit-email>...
#
# Canonical addresses are the account-bound GitHub noreply addresses where one
# exists, because a noreply address can only ever belong to the account it was
# issued for. A personal gmail address can be reassigned or reused by its owner,
# which would silently move commits onto whoever claims it later.
#
# Not mapped on purpose:
#   nathenbrewer@gmail.com and leo.camus23@gmail.com already cover both of that
#   person's display names, and GitHub matches on the email, so they already
#   collapse to a single contributor without help.

# Upstream author, whose commits span a personal address, a ChatGPT-assistant
# address, and their verified GitHub noreply.
Krishna Vishwakarma <88382789+Spyou@users.noreply.github.com> krishnavishwakarma2525@gmail.com
Krishna Vishwakarma <88382789+Spyou@users.noreply.github.com> chatgptkrylor@gmail.com

